+# Privacy by Design – The Daily Grind website
+
+This document is the engineering record of how the public website protects
+visitors. It is enforced by `npm run audit:privacy`, which runs as part of
+`npm run build` and fails the build on any violation.
+
+## 1. Data map (what a visit discloses, and to whom)
+
+| Data                               | Recipient            | Why / control                                                   |
+| ---------------------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| IP address, User-Agent, URL        | The Daily Grind only | Unavoidable to serve the page. No third party receives it.      |
+| Referrer when leaving the site     | Nobody               | `Referrer-Policy: same-origin` and `<meta name="referrer">`.    |
+| Cookies                            | None set client-side | Backend session cookies must be `__Host-`, `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict`. |
+| Browser storage                    | Tab-scoped session storage only | Namespaced `dg:`, expiring, blocked for personal-data keys, cleared on logout. |
+| Tracking parameters (`utm_*`, `fbclid`, `gclid`, …) | Stripped from the address bar on load | `assets/js/privacy.js` – they never reach history, bookmarks or logs via later navigation. |
+| Image metadata (EXIF/XMP)          | Removed from shipped images | Audit rule `assets/metadata`.                                    |
+
+Third parties currently approved to receive visitor requests: **none**
+(see `config/third-parties.json`).
+
+## 2. Markup rules (`index.html`)
+
+* All scripts and styles are external files on our origin. No inline
+  `<script>`, `<style>`, `style=""` or `on*=""` handlers, so the CSP does not
+  need `'unsafe-inline'`.
+* `<meta name="referrer" content="same-origin">` and a `<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy">`
+  fallback mirror the HTTP headers for hosts that cannot set headers. The
+  audit fails if they drift apart.
+* State-changing actions (logout) are `POST` forms, never `GET` links.
+* `rel="privacy-policy"` marks the privacy policy link for user agents.
+* No `preconnect` / `dns-prefetch` to other hosts; no third-party embeds.
+* The footer states the posture in plain language and shows a confirmation
+  when the browser sends a Global Privacy Control / Do Not Track signal.
+
+## 3. Client-side script (`assets/js/privacy.js`)
+
+The only script on the page. It never makes a network request and exposes a
+frozen `window.DailyGrindPrivacy` API:
+
+| Feature                      | Behaviour                                                                        |
+| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Tracking-parameter scrubbing | Removes known cross-site tracking query parameters via `history.replaceState`.  |
+| GPC / DNT                    | `optedOut()` returns `true`; the page announces that the signal is honoured.     |
+| Runtime third-party audit    | `PerformanceObserver` + `MutationObserver` flag any request to a non-approved origin (`privacy:third-party` event, console warning) and remove injected cross-origin `<script>`/`<iframe>` elements. |
+| Link hygiene                 | Adds `rel="noopener noreferrer"` and `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"` to external / `_blank` links. |
+| Safe storage                 | `storage.set/get/remove/clear`: session-only, namespaced, size-capped, expiring, refuses keys that look like personal data. |
+| Logout                       | Clears site storage and Cache Storage before the `POST /logout`; the server adds `Clear-Site-Data`. |
+
+The audit bans `document.cookie`, `localStorage`, `eval`, HTML string sinks,
+network APIs and fingerprinting APIs in anything under `assets/js/`. A future
+same-origin API call needs a deliberate exemption in the audit, reviewed
+alongside the data it sends.
+
+## 4. Security headers (`config/security-headers.json`)
+
+Defined once and rendered by `npm run build:headers` into `_headers`
+(Netlify / Cloudflare Pages) and `config/nginx-headers.conf`.
+
+| Header                                   | Value / purpose                                                               |
+| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Content-Security-Policy                  | `default-src 'none'`, each directive opened to `'self'` only; `frame-ancestors 'none'`; Trusted Types required. Blocks any injected third-party resource. |
+| Referrer-Policy                          | `same-origin`                                                                 |
+| Permissions-Policy                       | Disables sensors, camera, microphone, geolocation, payment, and the advertising APIs (`interest-cohort`, `browsing-topics`, `attribution-reporting`, `join-ad-interest-group`, `run-ad-auction`). |
+| Strict-Transport-Security                | 2 years, subdomains, preload.                                                 |
+| Cross-Origin-Opener/Embedder/Resource-Policy | Full cross-origin isolation; our assets cannot be embedded elsewhere.      |
+| X-Content-Type-Options / X-Frame-Options | `nosniff` / `DENY`                                                            |
+| Cache-Control                            | `no-store` for pages; long immutable cache for `/assets/*` (no personal data). |
+| Clear-Site-Data on `/logout`             | `"cache", "cookies", "storage"`                                               |
+
+Local development (`npm start`) passes the CSP and cross-origin isolation
+flags to `statikk`; the remaining headers are host-level and covered by the
+generated files above plus the `<meta>` fallbacks.
+
+## 5. Third-party audit procedure
+
+Nothing external may be loaded until it has passed this checklist and is
+recorded in `config/third-parties.json` under `approved`:
+
+1. **Necessity** – can the need be met first-party (self-host the asset, proxy the API)?
+2. **Data exposed** – list exactly what the browser will send (IP, UA, referrer, cookies, page URL, timing).
+3. **Legal basis and contract** – purpose, lawful basis, DPA signed, data location, retention.
+4. **Technical containment** – add the origin to the relevant CSP directive only
+   (never `*`), to `allowedOrigins` in `privacy.js`, use `crossorigin="anonymous"`
+   and `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`, and SRI hashes for scripts/styles.
+5. **Consent** – if the recipient could identify or profile visitors, load it
+   only after opt-in consent and never when GPC/DNT is set (`DailyGrindPrivacy.optedOut()`).
+6. **Review date** – set `nextReview`; expired entries should be removed.
+
+Removed third parties stay listed under `removed` for the record. The Unsplash
+hero image CDN was removed on 2026-10-28 and replaced with self-hosted,
+metadata-stripped copies.
+
+## 6. Commands
+
+```sh
+npm run build          # render headers + run the audit (CI gate)
+npm run audit:privacy  # audit only; add --json for machine-readable output
+npm run build:headers  # regenerate _headers and config/nginx-headers.conf
+npm start              # local server with CSP + cross-origin isolation
+```
